    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43746" root="&#xA;                        منى&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُمْنِيَّةٌ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>An object of wish,</i> or <i>desire:</i> originally,
<i>a thing that a man meditates</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يُقَدِّرُهُ</span>) in his mind;
from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَنَى</span> signifying <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَدَّرَ</span>: and hence applied to
a lie; and to what is wished, or desired, and
what is read, or desired [pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَمَانِىُّ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَمَانٍ</span>].
(Bd in ii. 73.) See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُنْبَةٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَجْوَى</span>.

